## re-capturing them as mode-160000 gitlinks, which makes actions/checkout fail
## ("fatal: No url found for submodule path ...") and breaks ALL CI. They have no
## real repo (~/git/<name> absent) and no tracked content. Formerly covered by the
## Added 2026-06-13.
## local ./gradlew left .gradle/ and build/ untracked-but-addable — and
## bb_flakes_termux/build.sh does `git add -A`. Same class of gap as the
## whitelist above, or the whitelist would drag libs/*/build/ back in.
## Gradle writes local.properties with a machine-local `sdk.dir` on every
## build. It must never be committed — it points at whatever SDK path that
## one machine had (here: /tmp/android-sdk) and breaks every other checkout
## and CI. There was NO rule for this anywhere until 2026-08-09;
## applies to all nine Android apps in this repo, so the rule is global
## rather than per-app. Nothing matching it is currently tracked.
local.properties
**/local.properties
