# ── Sibling working clones (were submodules until 2026-08-11) ────────────────
## cloud-master is the indexing path now: it holds committed RELATIVE symlinks
## out to working clones in ~/git, deliberately not submodules (a submodule
## pins a commit and wants --recursive, which meant cloud-master containing
## cloud containing cloud-master). unix no longer tracks these at all.
##
## They are still on disk here as ordinary clones and would otherwise show up
## as untracked forever. Ignoring them keeps `git status` honest without
## deleting anything. Nothing in unix reads through these paths at runtime.
##
## Do NOT re-add these to 0_git/src/gitmodules — the ship engine
## reconciles from that file and would resurrect them as submodules.
/I_cloud-data/
/II_tools/
/III_front-data/
/IV_cloud-configs/
/V_front-configs/

## ── dtk: content that generic ignore rules would swallow ──────────
## dtk arrived from the standalone cloud-mykonsole-dtk repo (2026-08-26)
## where `build/` and `libs/` are REAL source, not build output:
##   build/git-workflows + build/flake-engines are the dtk build engine,
##   commands/connect/dashboard/libs is vendored dashboard code.
## `build/` is ignored by the USER-GLOBAL ~/.config/git/ignore, and `libs/`
## by this file, so a plain `git add dtk` silently drops 39 files with no
## error. Un-ignoring the DIRECTORY is required — git cannot re-include a
## file whose parent directory is excluded.
!/dtk/build/
!/dtk/.archive/a-Git/build/
!/dtk/commands/connect/dashboard/libs/
